> Is it correct to prefer the std.lv <http://std.lv> ( or std.nox) estimates over std.all when interpreting the regression coefficients of dummy-coded variables as standardized mean differences?

std.nox is like std.all, except the exogenous predictors are not standardized.  That sounds most appropriate for interpreting effect sizes of dummy-coded predictors, whose SD is not a meaningful "unit" of measurement.

